# BUILD BRIEF: "Sunway Hub" – an unofficial, non-commercial study resources and campus events website for Sunway University students

You are a senior full-stack engineer. Build the complete website described below. Work in phases (see "Build order"), run tests after each phase, and summarise what you built before moving on. If something is ambiguous, pick the safer and simpler option and list it under "Assumptions" at the end instead of stopping to ask.

## 1. What this is
- A closed, members-only website for the Sunway University community (students, teachers, staff) to share study notes, find club info, and see campus events.
- It is a student-run, UNOFFICIAL project. It is NOT affiliated with or endorsed by Sunway University. Show this disclaimer in the footer of every page and in the Terms.
- It is strictly NON-COMMERCIAL. No ads, no payments, no donations, no sponsorships, no paid features, no marketplace, no affiliate links, and no third-party tracking or analytics. The owner is an international student on a Malaysian student pass, so any income-generating feature is forbidden. Do not add any, even as a placeholder.
- Language: English only. No language switcher, no i18n framework.
- Do not use the Sunway logo, brand colours or mascots anywhere. Use a plain text wordmark "Sunway Hub".

## 2. Infrastructure: VERCEL AND NEON ONLY
Use only these two platforms. Do NOT use or suggest Supabase, Firebase, AWS services directly, Upstash/Redis, Cloudflare, Resend, Sentry, or any other hosted service.
- Hosting and server: Vercel (Hobby plan, which is for non-commercial use). Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS. Set the function region to Singapore (sin1) if available, to stay close to Malaysia.
- Database: Neon Postgres (pick the Singapore region). Use Drizzle ORM with the `@neondatabase/serverless` driver and versioned migrations. Use a pooled connection string for the app.
- File storage: Vercel Blob, using a PRIVATE store only (never public). Files are served only through an authenticated route that checks the session and approval status, or through short-lived signed URLs.
- Scheduled jobs: Vercel Cron, protected by a `CRON_SECRET` header. Design all jobs to run once per day (Hobby plan limits), and make them idempotent.
- Email: Neither Vercel nor Neon sends email. Use `nodemailer` with Gmail SMTP (a dedicated Gmail account with 2-step verification and an app password) behind a small `sendEmail()` interface, so the provider can be swapped later by changing one file. This is the ONLY allowed external dependency, and it must be documented as such in the Privacy Policy and README.
- Everything else is built in-app with npm packages: authentication, sessions, rate limiting (counters stored in Neon), search (Postgres full-text search with `tsvector` and `pg_trgm`), image processing (`sharp`), TOTP (`otplib`), password hashing (`@node-rs/argon2`), validation (`zod`), and the bad-word filter.
- Tests: Vitest for unit tests, Playwright for a few end-to-end tests.
- Authorisation is enforced on the SERVER in one central data-access layer. Every query and mutation goes through functions that take the current user and check role, ownership and approval status. Never rely on hidden buttons or client-side checks. Add tests that prove a normal member cannot read or modify other people's pending content or reach admin functions.
- Provide `.env.example` with: DATABASE_URL, BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN (not needed when Vercel's automatic OIDC auth is available), SESSION_SECRET, OTP_PEPPER, ADMIN_EMAIL, ALLOWED_EMAIL_DOMAINS, SMTP_USER, SMTP_APP_PASSWORD, SMTP_FROM, CRON_SECRET, APP_URL, STORAGE_CAP_GB.

## 3. Design system (minimal, flat, NO gradients)
- No gradients anywhere. No glassmorphism, blur, neon, glow, or decorative shadows. No stock illustrations. No emojis in the UI.
- Flat solid colours only. Palette: background #FFFFFF, surface #F7F7F8, text #111111, muted text #6B7280, border #E5E7EB, one accent colour #1D4ED8 for primary buttons and links, danger #B91C1C, success #15803D.
- Separate elements with 1px borders and whitespace, not shadows. Border radius 6px. 8px spacing grid.
- Font: Inter, self-hosted (no Google Fonts requests), with a system sans-serif fallback. Max 3 text sizes in body content.
- Icons: Lucide line icons only, used sparingly.
- Mobile-first and fully responsive (most students will use phones). WCAG 2.1 AA: visible focus rings, colour contrast, keyboard navigation, alt text on images, labelled form fields.
- Light theme only. Clear empty states, loading skeletons (flat grey, no shimmer gradient), and friendly error messages. Include 404 and 500 pages.
- Dates shown as "12 Oct 2026", times in 24-hour format, timezone Asia/Kuala_Lumpur.

