## 5. Login page (simple) and custom authentication
One centred card with: the "Sunway Hub" wordmark, one email field, a "Continue" button, and small links to Terms and Privacy. Nothing else.

Flow after the email is submitted:
1. If the email is `ADMIN_EMAIL`:
   - First time ever (no password set): send a 6-digit one-time code to that email. After the code is verified, show "Create your password" (min 12 characters, strength meter, reject common passwords). Store only an Argon2id hash. From then on the admin signs in with email + password.
   - After a password exists: ask for the password. Offer "Forgot password" (one-time code to the admin email). Strongly encourage TOTP two-factor authentication and require re-entering the password before sensitive admin actions.
   - Admin sessions expire after 12 hours of inactivity.
2. If the email domain is in `ALLOWED_EMAIL_DOMAINS`: send a 6-digit one-time code (valid 10 minutes, single use, max 5 attempts). No passwords for members. Session lasts 30 days on that device.
3. Anything else: show "Only Sunway email addresses can sign in." Use the same neutral wording and response timing in all failure cases so the site never reveals which emails exist.
- Rate limit by IP and by email (e.g. 5 code requests per hour per email), with counters stored in Neon.
- Only the admin email can ever have a password. There must be no code path that creates or accepts a password for any other account.

Implementation notes:
- Store one-time codes only as hashes (SHA-256 with `OTP_PEPPER`), with expiry and attempt counters. Invalidate old codes when a new one is issued.
- Sessions live in a Neon `sessions` table. The cookie holds a random token (stored hashed), is httpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Lax, and rotates on login. Support "sign out everywhere" and admin force-sign-out.
- Do not use any third-party auth service.

First-login onboarding (members, one-time, cannot skip):
- Accept Terms and Privacy Policy via an unticked checkbox. Store the document versions and timestamp.
- Choose a username, display name, role (student / teacher / other) and pronouns (he / she / rather not say). Profile picture and bio are optional.

## 6. Profiles
Fields: full name, username, bio, email, profile picture, pronouns, role.
- Username: unique, 3-20 characters, lowercase letters, numbers and underscores only, may be changed once every 30 days, reserved words blocked (admin, support, sunway, moderator, etc.). The bad-word filter applies.
- Bio: max 160 characters. Bad-word filter applies.
- Pronouns: exactly three options: "he", "she", "rather not say" (default). Show "he" or "she" on the profile only if chosen; show nothing for "rather not say".
- Role: student / teacher / other. Choosing "teacher" shows a "Teacher (pending verification)" label only to the owner and admin. The public sees a "Verified teacher" badge only after the admin verifies it. Verification never grants extra permissions; it is a trust badge and does not skip approval.
- Email: always visible to the owner and admin. Public visibility is a toggle on the profile, DEFAULT HIDDEN.
- Profile picture: JPG, PNG or WebP, max 2 MB, uploaded through a server route, auto-cropped to a square 512x512 and re-encoded with `sharp` (this strips EXIF metadata). It must be APPROVED BY ADMIN before the public sees it. Until approved, the public sees a flat grey initials avatar, while the owner sees their new picture with a "Pending approval" label. If rejected, the owner is notified with a reason and the old approved picture (or initials) remains. Changing a picture again starts a new approval and keeps the previous approved one visible meanwhile.
- Profile page shows: picture, name, @username, pronouns, role/badge, bio, email (if public), join date, and a tab listing the user's approved posts. The owner also sees tabs for Pending, Rejected and Bookmarks.
- Account settings: edit profile, email visibility, notification preferences, download my data (JSON), delete my account (confirm with a code; choose either to delete my posts too, or to keep them anonymised as "Deleted user").

## 7. Posts
Post types: Study Material, Event, Club Post.
Fields: title (required, 5-100 characters), description (up to 2000 characters), type, subject tag (course/subject code or name, with autocomplete from existing tags), semester (e.g. "Jan 2026"), optional club, attachments.

Attachments and upload flow (Vercel Blob, private store):
- Allowed: images (JPG, PNG, WebP, max 10 MB each), PDF (max 25 MB), DOCX/PPTX (max 25 MB), video MP4 (max 50 MB). Up to 10 files per post.
- Use Vercel Blob CLIENT UPLOADS (the browser uploads directly after the server authorises it), because serverless request bodies are too small for large files. The authorisation step checks the session, the daily quota, the storage cap, allowed content types and the maximum size, and issues a token for a path under `quarantine/{userId}/...`.
- A finalise step on the server then verifies the real file type by content (magic bytes, not extension), re-encodes images with `sharp` to strip EXIF, computes a SHA-256 hash to detect duplicates, and only then records the file against the post. Files that fail are deleted from Blob immediately. Orphaned quarantine files are deleted by the daily cron job.
- Files are never reachable by a public URL. Serve them through an authenticated route (or a short-lived signed URL) that confirms: the viewer is logged in, and the post is approved (or the viewer is the owner or admin).
- Upload quotas: 10 uploads per day and 200 MB total per user, configurable by admin. The Hobby Blob allowance is shared and shared storage can stop working if the limit is exceeded, so add a global storage guard: env `STORAGE_CAP_GB`, an admin storage meter, a warning at 80%, and automatic refusal of new uploads at 90%.
- Malware scanning is not available in this stack. Instead, restrict file types strictly, never execute or render uploaded HTML, and serve downloads with `Content-Disposition: attachment` and `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`.

Rules:
- Before submitting, the uploader must tick: "This is my own work, or I have permission to share it. It is not a lecturer's slides, a textbook, an exam paper, exam answers, or assessment material for a currently running assessment."
- APPROVAL REQUIRED FOR EVERY UPLOAD. Status flow: pending -> approved | rejected | changes_requested. Only approved posts are visible to other members. The poster sees their own pending, rejected and changes-requested posts with the admin's reason. Admin posts are auto-approved.
- Poster permissions: may EDIT THE TITLE ONLY. Description, tags, semester and attachments (images, videos, files) are locked after submission; to change them, delete and repost. Title edits must pass the bad-word filter, show an "edited" label, store the previous title in an edit history visible to admin, and be revertible by admin. Add an admin setting "Require re-approval after title edit" (default off).
- Delete: the poster can delete their own post, and the admin can delete any post (admin must enter a reason, which is sent to the poster). Deletion is soft first (hidden immediately), with permanent purge of the database rows and Blob files after 30 days by the daily cron job. Log every deletion in the audit log.
- Member actions on approved posts: "Helpful" vote (one per user, removable), bookmark, report, share link (works only for logged-in members).
- Report button on every post, profile, club, event: reason categories (copyright, inappropriate, harassment, exam/cheating material, spam, other) + optional note. Content with 3+ open reports from different users is auto-hidden pending admin review.
- Browsing: Home feed (newest approved), Subjects pages (organised by subject tag and semester), full-text search (Postgres) with filters (type, subject, semester, verified teacher, club), sort by newest / most helpful, pagination. Keep large text and metadata in Neon and files in Blob, to stay within the Neon storage allowance.

