## 9. Bad-word filtering (applies EVERYWHERE)
Block profanity in every text input: names, usernames, bios, post titles and descriptions, title edits, club and event text, report notes, contact form, club manager requests, any future comment or Q&A text, and uploaded file names.
- Run the check on the server (authoritative) and in the browser (for instant feedback). A client-side check alone is never enough.
- Use a maintained library (for example `obscenity` for JavaScript) and add: English profanity, common Malay profanity, and common transliterated Arabic, Chinese and Tamil insults used in Malaysia. Normalise text before checking: Unicode normalisation, lowercase, strip accents, collapse repeated characters, convert leetspeak (@ -> a, 0 -> o, $ -> s, 1 -> i), and ignore inserted spaces, dots and symbols. Use word-boundary logic to avoid false positives on innocent words (the "Scunthorpe problem"), e.g. "class", "assess", "Essex".
- On a hit, block the submission and show: "Please remove inappropriate language and try again." Do not say which word triggered it.
- Admin page "Blocked words": view, add, remove and import words, and an allow-list for false positives. Changes apply instantly (stored in Neon, cached briefly in memory).
- Unit-test the filter with at least 50 cases (obfuscated spellings, innocent words, other languages).
- Images and videos cannot be word-filtered, so they depend on admin approval and on reports. Add an optional adapter for an image-moderation API, disabled by default.

