## 12. Security and quality requirements
- Central server-side authorisation layer (see section 2). Every API route and server action re-checks the session and role.
- Zod validation on all inputs; output encoding to prevent XSS; CSRF protection for all mutations; strict Content-Security-Policy and other security headers; no third-party scripts, fonts or trackers.
- Rate limiting (counters in Neon) on login, uploads, reports, search and contact.
- Private Blob storage only; never expose raw storage paths.
- Do not log email addresses, one-time codes or file contents in application logs.
- Backups: rely on Neon's built-in restore features, and also provide the admin "full export" in section 10. Document the restore procedure in the README.
- Unit tests: email-domain matching (including lookalikes), admin-only rules, profanity filter, upload validation, post permissions (poster can edit the title only), and authorisation tests proving members cannot access other users' pending content or admin functions. E2E tests: login (member and admin first-time), post upload -> approval -> visible, profile picture approval, delete by poster and by admin.
- Accessibility check with axe on the main pages.

